# HANDOVER, not a falsifier. These claims fail today and cannot fall further,
# which is the second hole the php lane left open and is said out loud here
# rather than discovered later: this file cannot tell a break from a baseline.
# It exists to price the seat and to name the mechanism.
#
# `=~` inside `[[ … ]]` takes `_regex_no_space`, aliased to `regex` - one of
# three terminals bash's scanner serves from one function on `valid_symbols`,
# which is php's family *surface* and not php's mechanism.
#
# What the C actually does, per byte, is keep THREE independent depth counters
# (paren, bracket, brace) plus an in-single-quote flag, and stop on the first
# closer that would go negative. `marrow` walks to a close the roster names;
# there is no close here to name. The other half is a refusal on the matched
# text rather than on what follows: a run of only `[A-Za-z0-9$_-]` is a word and
# not a regex, so `found_non_alnumdollarunderdash` gates the return.
#
# It also does not fit `Provision`. A pattern can carry depth-1 nesting, but the
# C refuses `$(` mid-run on purpose - `// do not parse a command substitution` -
# so the grammar's own `command_substitution` can take it. A linear pattern has
# no way to say "a `$` that is not followed by `(`", and eating it would build a
# confidently wrong node where we currently build none. That is the whole reason
# this is left blind rather than approximated.
#
# Priced on the corpus, so the next lane starts from a measurement: `ledger.sh`
# holds one regex, `^-?[0-9]+$`, and the board's `unexpected [ at 565` is the
# `[` of that `[0-9]` - NOT the `[[` of the test command, and not `_concat`.
# bash's whole damage is 413 bytes and this is the wall inside it.
